A project declares its items in `.claude/skilletor.json`; skilletor installs them wherever a session works in that project, with no `skilletor sync` by hand.

## What happens today

skilletor's hooks look at the session's project dir only (`CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`): SessionStart syncs it at start, UserPromptSubmit on its interval. A session that moves mid-session into another checkout of a skilletor project works there without that checkout's installed items (`.claude/skills/<installed>`, `.claude/rules/.local.*`, `.claude/agents/.local.*`, the lock). The usual case is a worktree made with plain `git worktree add`: git copies tracked files only, and `.worktreeinclude` applies only to worktrees Claude Code creates itself.

Seen 2026-11-10 in p5-mcp-hub: the session ran `git worktree add .claude/worktrees/backlog`, then `cd` into it, and briefing denied every agent spawned there:

    briefing: agent 'mcp-hub-worker' references unknown skill(s): getty-perl-core, perl-mojo, perl-mcp, docker, kanban-issues-karr-ticket, getty-perl-pod

A session *started* in such a worktree is fine: its SessionStart check sees the missing lock and syncs (verified: 2 skills before, 14 skills and the lock after `skilletor hook session-start`).

## The hook

Claude Code 2.1.322 has the hook event `CwdChanged` ("After the working directory changes"). Its input carries `old_cwd` and `new_cwd`; its output takes `systemMessage` and `hookSpecificOutput: {hookEventName: "CwdChanged", watchPaths?}`. It fires on a plain Bash `cd` (verified with a project hook in a `claude -p` run: `cd sub` delivered `{"hook_event_name":"CwdChanged","old_cwd":"…/cwdtest","new_cwd":"…/cwdtest/sub", …}`).

## Done when

- `hooks/hooks.json` registers `CwdChanged` → `skilletor hook cwd-changed`.
- On a move into a checkout (git top level of `new_cwd`) that has its own `.claude/skilletor.json`, skilletor brings that checkout's project scope up to date the way SessionStart does (same timeout, same trust rules: a move never trusts a backend) and says so in one line naming the directory, e.g. `skilletor: 17 item(s) updated in <dir>`.
- A move within the same checkout, or into a directory without a skilletor project, stays cheap: no source round trip per `cd`. A checkout whose lock already matches its config is left alone (remote changes keep coming through the existing interval check).
- When it cannot sync (untrusted source, offline, config error), the line says so and names the fix for that directory (`skilletor trust <name>` / `skilletor sync` in `<dir>`), like the SessionStart warning.
- Measured and noted on this card: does Claude Code wait for the CwdChanged hook before the next tool call runs (a `cd`, then an Agent spawn in the next call)? If not, what the window is and how the design covers it.
- Tests in `test/` for: worktree without lock → synced; same checkout → no sync; directory without skilletor project → no-op; untrusted source → warning, nothing fetched.
- Spec (hooks section) and the user docs (`README.md`, `skills/skilletor` references) describe the event. Codex and Hermes have no such event — say so; the Perl port gets the same change or the divergence is noted here.
- `npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run build && npm run check-dist` green, `dist/skilletor.js` rebuilt in the same commit.

